 this world fairly easily but that  would not result in permanent change  instead gojo prefers the philosophy of  generational revolution  much much much slower but also much much  much more powerful so he focuses very  much on fostering yuji and the other  students to one day inherit the world  with his ideals in mind which is  interesting because it's a direct  counterpoint to the other cursed spirit  dude whose name is jogo  which you know in japanese is just gojo  backwards but his idea is the more  traditionally  violent revolution in order to install a  power structure of what i believe he  called  new humans which is a fascinating term  because for lack of a better and  or more creative word it humanizes these  cursed spirits through jogo's eyes or i  singular they are just an evolution of  humanity it blurs these once distinct  lines of evil  curse dudes and i hope that jujutsu  kaisen continues to do so as well and  with that said yuji is of course the  perfect vessel for that kind of  discussion because he is currently the  amalgamation of a human and a cursed  spirit so the inner conflict within yuji  may just be a simplistic incarnation of  global conflict at large  that or i am just reading far too much  into things which  can happen but even if that was the case  i like that jujutakaisen is engaging me  in this way now speaking of engaging by  far the best part of this arc for me was  the rapid expansion of curse mechanics  another thing that didn't really quite  hit with me in the previous arc was  being thrust into this curse-based  scenario and not really having any idea  how things function outside of this kind  of simplistic grading system so the  whole dump truck of concepts and  information was absurdly valuable to me  during the sock and i now see why people  kept insisting that jujutsu kaisen was  similar to hunter hunter in terms of the  power system aspect on a very basic  level it does appear at this stage  anyway to function quite similarly to  nen which i want to emphasize  is not a bad thing not a bad thing at  all i still think that nen is the  greatest power system ever invented in  pretty much all of media so curses being  similar to nen can only infinitely  benefit  jutsukai sen in my opinion but if i  understand this correctly  and to be fair i may not but one can  manifest cursed energy as a direct  response to emotion  specifically negative emotion and with  that energy you can then construct a  curse technique  so yeah quite similar to using aura to  forge your fuel none abilities but i am  intrigued by the idea that this energy  can only be spawned through negative  emotions not  positive ones i love that thought so  much because it's just so damn twisted  like i don't know this might be wrong  but right now to me what this signifies  is that the stronger of a jujuta  sorcerer you are the more you need to  inhabit that place of pure pain  let's take gojo for example dude is an  insanely powerful sorcerer so just how  negative do his emotions need to be in  order to produce that energy like what  kind of hell has this man been through  to land at this place of power and i  guess that makes sense because it really  isn't a casual content thought  you don't want to instigate a fun little  revolution that and his raw hatred of  those currently in charge being on full  display make me wonder just how dark  this man truly is behind his comical  facade and i suppose that's also how  yuji could really break the mould in  jiu-jitsu kaisen  being this insanely positive personality  that draws more from sukuna's power than  the negative emotions of his own i  know it's just a fun stuff to think  about as is another vaguely explored  mechanic being the binding vow it was  very exciting to see that whole section  happen because of course it immediately  gave me flashbacks of setting nen vows  and n restrictions which almost always  results in the most fascinating of hunt  hunter abilities so i'm very keen to  explore these vowels and i'm also very  glad to know that yes crazy power can be  achieved but it will come at a cost  whether that be through a vowel or just  needing to fuel mental negativity to  achieve more and more energy this whole  system seems incredibly high risk  high reward and of course i should  mention the particularly unique feature  introduced to us during the sock being  domain expansion i really enjoy this  because we've got to see what like four  domains this arc gojos jogos sukunas and  the mysterious antagonist character with  like the other messed up face  but i like these because domains appear  to be not just a cool way to fight but  also a direct manifestation of character  take gojo for example once again because  he is the best example of anything but  his domain was essentially  infinite of all of the things however  when faced with the ability to access  absolutely everything you become unable  to do anything which i don't know is the  idea that without limitations and any  form of decision making just becomes  impossible like a more extreme version  of going out to dinner with a friend and  being unable to choose a restaurant  because there's just like a billion  around you and neither of you are  decisive but this also seems to be very  representative of what i know of gojo  himself in reality he seems like this  man with limitless power but he also  can't use it due to his personal  philosophy of change i mean just imagine  that being the undisputed most powerful  force in the world and having all of  that power being utterly meaningless  when it comes to enacting the thing it  is you want to do meanwhile there are  much more simplistic domains as well  like jogos which was just  i'm in angry cyclops dude so my domain  is fiery and violent there they're there  but the idea of domain versus domain  combat is just this epic amped up battle  of i suppose two personalities  it's cool and it will make me pay a lot  of attention to 