aracter to go from like level  100 to 150 at that point fatigue sets in  and it can seem like a bit of a grind so  i think that jujutsu kaisen has handled  this pretty perfectly thus far with some  great action as well with  gojo versus jo go and actually that's a  pretty big thing i should bring up we  see gojo's eyes oh my god they are  surprisingly  stunningly beautiful not at all what i  was expecting and i'd be keen to know  why he wears the blindfold in everyday  life my initial thinking is that this  would be a binding vowel or whatever  setting a restriction that he can't use  his eyes outside of his domain in  exchange for making his domain more  powerful or for it to be capable of  existing in the first place  and speaking of fights yes i've mostly  glossed over it until now but yuji  vsukuna was quite something as well  in the uh the corpsey inner domain it  was interesting because it was quite  clear that tsukuna was always in control  but what  really hit me was round two when yuji  fought for the right to be brought back  to life with no restrictions and then  tsukino just sliced his head in two  whilst yuji was still speaking which i  imagine is a mere glimpse of sukuna's  true power and what was happening  previously was more akin to an adult  humoring a child  because part of me did think that yeah  eugene might actually be doing well in  this place because he is a crazy  superhuman after all but no all yuji hit  was the infinity between them and i  guess that brings us back to gojo  because i really love that infinity  concept the idea that the closer you get  to him the more you slow down and thus  it makes it impossible to ever really  you know hit him it very much reminds me  of a stand in part six of jojo's bizarre  adventure called green green grass of  home which had a very similar idea  except the closer you get to it the more  you shrunk and thus you would never be  able to reach it because the distance  always remains the same and i bring 